const body = `COMPLETE REPRESENTABILITY (Wave 4 / divRep) — START HERE \`agent-ready\`

GOAL: land \`divRep\` (Div^g-lite representable), then the datum tail, concluding \`AJCR.w4-rep\` (Pic^0 representability). Orient from roadmap node \`AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr\` and the earlier inbox trail \`I-0289…I-0307\`.

AUDITED STATE (2026-07-20): the previous handoff’s claim that only a bounded total-stalk bridge remained is false. The chart reading map has an \`R\`-linear range \`P\`; RD-N concerns the genuine chart ideal \`J = B · P\`, where \`B = Γ(V)\`. The landed flatness is flatness of \`B/P\` as an \`R\`-module, not purity or flatness of \`B/J\` after quotienting by a chosen section.

Guard example: \`R = k[ε]/(ε²)\`, \`B = R[t]\`, \`P = R·t + R·(t²+ε)\`, \`s=t\`. The reduced fibre is generated by \`t\` and \`B/P\` is \`R\`-free, but \`J/(s)=(ε)\) has nonzero fibre at \`(ε,t)\`. Thus an achiever and a total-stalk lift alone cannot prove RD-N.

CORRECT CRITICAL PATH: use the second Grassmannian window to prove relative multiplication persistence \`K' = H_s · K\) from P-fib in every residue field, globalize fibre-surjectivity by finite-module Nakayama, then prove the resulting ideal-level purity/local principality. Only then derive \`SeedUnivRDN\`/unconditional \`isGenerator\` → certificate/U1 → F5/F6/F7 → \`divRep\`.

VALID LANDED INFRASTRUCTURE: residue-point lift \`abac842cc\` (\`DivSchemeFibrePoint.lean\`); sharp single-point \`κ(z)\` consumer \`ca7c437d4\`; genuine \`chartReadIdeal\` and equality with the old colength module \`e0a718b0c\`; finite fibre-surjectivity/Nakayama globalization \`b67d9b09\`, \`77e1f3bd\`. The draft Quot/FGA project is typed-sorry dependent and is not a complete shortcut.

BINDING: stay single-point for the RD-N consumer, but do not mistake single-point fibre divisibility for ideal purity; do not reuse the old chart-flat inference or the dead global \`κ(p)\) bridge.`;
